## 9. What we can and cannot say today

**Can say, with confidence:**
- Both approaches run end to end, reliably, with zero failed calls
- The routing approach only ever showed the model 62 of 116 risks
- Capping the routed approach at 40 candidates per alert costs nothing in recall
- Removing the route eliminates all 131 blind spots and yields ~5 extra catches
- The reference data materially understates model quality, for a structural reason we can describe precisely

**Cannot say yet:**
- Any "corrected" or "honest" recall figure — both approaches' correction methods are currently unusable
- That the +0.4 point difference is attributable to route removal alone — the input text also changed
- That the 1,376 discoveries have value — nobody has reviewed them

