## 11. Plain-English glossary

| Term | What it means |
|---|---|
| **Golden dataset** | The hand-verified list of known-correct links. Our reference for "right answers". Incomplete by design. |
| **Recall** | Of the known-correct links, what share did we find? |
| **Discovery** | A link the model predicted that isn't in the golden. Possibly a genuine link nobody recorded. Not an error. |
| **Never judged** | A known-correct link the model was never shown, so it had no chance to find it. |
| **Structural over-mapping** | The golden marking a link only because the risk sits under a regulation the alert touched — not because the documents support it. |
| **Correct rejection** | The model declined to link, and was right to. |
| **Top-k** | A cap on how many candidate risks each alert is checked against. |
| **Addressable** | Links the model could in principle find — i.e. the risk has published text. |

